From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Cather <mattbob4@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 14:00:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] libsanitizer: no glibc malloc extensions in HWASan on musl

HWASan aliases the glibc malloc extensions pvalloc, cfree, mallinfo,
mallopt and malloc_stats on every Linux target. ASan gates them on
glibc or Android. On musl none of the five exist in libc, so
libhwasan becomes their only provider and autoconf link tests report
them as present. Packages then compile their glibc code path and
fail, because the musl malloc.h declares neither mallopt nor
M_TRIM_THRESHOLD.

Gate the aliases the way ASan does. glibc and Android keep every
alias they have today. memalign stays outside the new guard: musl
provides it, so the tagged allocator has to keep serving those
allocations.

Signed-off-by: Matthew Cather <mattbob4@gmail.com>
---
 libsanitizer/hwasan/hwasan_allocation_functions.cpp |    4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/libsanitizer/hwasan/hwasan_allocation_functions.cpp
+++ b/libsanitizer/hwasan/hwasan_allocation_functions.cpp
@@ -182,10 +182,14 @@ INTERCEPTOR_ALIAS(void *, malloc, SIZE_T
 
 #  if !SANITIZER_FREEBSD && !SANITIZER_NETBSD
 INTERCEPTOR_ALIAS(void *, memalign, SIZE_T alignment, SIZE_T size);
+#  endif
+
+// Absent from musl libc; ASan gates these on SI_GLIBC || SI_ANDROID.
+#  if SANITIZER_GLIBC || SANITIZER_ANDROID
 INTERCEPTOR_ALIAS(void *, pvalloc, SIZE_T size);
 INTERCEPTOR_ALIAS(void, cfree, void *ptr);
 INTERCEPTOR_ALIAS(__sanitizer_struct_mallinfo, mallinfo);
 INTERCEPTOR_ALIAS(int, mallopt, int cmd, int value);
 INTERCEPTOR_ALIAS(void, malloc_stats, void);
 #  endif
 #endif  // #if HWASAN_WITH_INTERCEPTORS
